# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Red-team run artifacts
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# A run artifact contains full attack payloads plus whatever the target echoed
# back, which on a real engagement can include credentials it was holding or
# customer data. It is engagement evidence, not source. Attach it to the ticket
# that authorized the work; do not commit it.
runs/
*.run.json
*.run.jsonl
*.sarif

# Authorization records name systems, people, and escalation contacts. Keep the
# signed record with the engagement paperwork; commit only the example.
authorization.json
!examples/authorization.example.json

# The init-scaffolded engagement config points at the operator's systems and
# references their local corpus. Same class of local artifact as the record.
redteam.config.json

# Operator-supplied probe corpora (harm-category prompts, licensed benchmark
# sets). These are exactly what must not reach a public repository.
*.local.jsonl
*.local.json

# Local engagement working docs (counter payloads, per-target playbooks).
# Same class of engagement evidence as the corpora above.
*.local.md
*.local.py

# Local agent-state directories. Project-scoped skills remain committable
# (ignore children, not the dir itself, so the negation can apply).
.omc/*
.omo/
!.omc/skills/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Private research working logs
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Populated run logs must NOT be committed. Store full payload text here; commit
# only the blank template. Enforced by the safety.gitignore and
# safety.run_log_blank checks in redteam.datacheck.
*.local.csv
data/*.local.csv

# Full jailbreak conversations + Chrome session cookies — engagement evidence,
# never commit.
arena/gs-scrape.local/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Python
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.coverage
htmlcov/
